<http://digistrucmed.org/entity/patients%20with%20grade%202%20hypertension%20or%20higher> <http://digistrucmed.org/hasSourceMention> <http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/lu_1d4ae21bdadbacafa8087e019976dde180c346c5d4626772c2b286528336efac_n0056/e_0018> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/grade-record/lu_1d4ae21bdadbacafa8087e019976dde180c346c5d4626772c2b286528336efac_n0056/gr_0017> <http://digistrucmed.org/gradeSourceText> "I" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_1d4ae21bdadbacafa8087e019976dde180c346c5d4626772c2b286528336efac_n0056/tu_0002> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "It is recommended to base the diagnosis of hypertension on:\nRepeated office BP measurements, on more than one visit, except when hypertension is severe (e.g. grade 3 and especially in high-risk patients)\nor\nOut-of-office BP measurement with ABPM and/or HBPM when feasible." .
<http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/lu_1d4ae21bdadbacafa8087e019976dde180c346c5d4626772c2b286528336efac_n0056/e_0034> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://digistrucmed.org/Population> .
